{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC4 SATISFIED — the change LANDED.\n\n  Gerrit change: 1943  (https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/c/rebar/+/1943)\n  Change-Id:     I8e052b41c2ea4ca581633aec2be06deb65b0c41a\n  Merged sha:    dab851c5fb53db4e2cd63e49a305997e4db48f3b\n  Merged at:     2026-08-20 03:55:43 UTC, status MERGED, now the tip of main\n  Subject:       deps: bump the uv-lock group (dependabot PR #131)\n\nGate votes at submit time:\n  LLM-Review  +1  (rebar review bot — 'LLM-Review: PASS, rebar code review passed')\n  Verified    +1  (GitHub Actions run 32327898445, conclusion: success)\n  unresolved comments: 0\n  submittable: true\nSubmitted with a plain Gerrit Submit as RebarBotNava (Contributor). No recheck, no force, no pre-rebase needed.\n\nWHOLE-TREE VALIDATION (not just tests/unit). CI run 32327898445 ran the full default suite on the patchset across the whole matrix, all green:\n  pytest ubuntu-latest py3.11  success\n  pytest ubuntu-latest py3.12  success\n  pytest ubuntu-latest py3.13  success\n  pytest macos-latest  py3.13  success\n  lint + type-check            success\n  pip-audit                    success\n  golden-path (clean install)  success\n  artifact-probe / provenance  success\n  optionality (lean core wheel + per-extra venvs)  success\n  bounded mutation gates (gates, reducer-processors, compact-policy, validate, next-batch, signing, push-policy)  all success\n\nLocal pre-push validation covered the tree in chunks (the machine runs the suite serially, ~3h end to end):\n  tests/e2e                        12 passed\n  tests/integration + tests/scripts 1097 passed, 2 skipped\n  tests/interfaces                 clean through 59% before the runner was reaped, zero failures\n  tests/unit                       covered by the CI matrix above\n\nMETHOD NOTE for future agents: running the suite detached via nohup produces SPURIOUS errors that do not reproduce in a normal foreground shell. Two tests/e2e bpmn-io browser tests and tests/integration/test_reclaim_bridge_history.py::test_partial_clone_refusal_names_fresh_unfiltered_clone_remedy errored under nohup with stdin at /dev/null, then all passed when re-run in the foreground (tests/e2e 12 passed; that integration file 6 passed). Do not treat a detached-run error as a real failure without re-running it in the foreground."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787198181001299001,"uuid":"9ff5eaf4-77f3-47ed-8ad0-531297eb3a4e"}